  "worked_solution": "Dividing a whole number by a fraction is equivalent to multiplying the whole number by the reciprocal of the fraction.\n\nFirst, we write $9$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n9=\\frac{9}{1}\n$$\n\nNext, we note that the reciprocal of $\\frac{2}{3}$ is $\\frac{3}{2}.$ \n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n9÷\\frac{2}{3}=\\frac{9}{1}÷\\frac{2}{3}=\\frac{9}{1}\\times \\frac{3}{2}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply our fractions. \n\n$$\n\\frac{9}{1}\\times \\frac{3}{2}=\\frac{9\\times 3}{1\\times 2}=\\frac{27}{2}\n$$",
